 "title": "C. albicans Metabolic Pathways and Gene Regulation",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around Candida albicans, an organism with various metabolic pathways and gene regulations. Met32, a gene or protein, plays a central role in regulating methionine biosynthesis and interacting with other genes and proteins. C. albicans also utilizes RSS and has upregulated transcripts for sulfur assimilation and methionine synthase. Additionally, the organism has pathogenic relationships with sulfur amino acid biosynthetic pathways and has genes for Met30 and Met31. The cluster also includes other organisms, such as Aspergillus fumigatus and Cryptococcus neoformans, which have pathogenic relationships with sulfur amino acid biosynthetic pathways. Chemicals like GSH and GSSG are also present, with GSH being imported by C. albicans and Francisella novicida.",
